# The domain comes from SPLOUCH_DOMAIN in cloud/.env — do not write it in here.
#
# This file is tracked by git. A deploy that resets the working tree (the Update
# button's master and branch modes) reverts anything edited here, so a literal domain
# would silently go back to the placeholder and Caddy would serve the wrong site — and
# fail to renew the certificate — from its next restart. `.env` is untracked, so the
# domain survives every update.
#
# Caddy obtains and renews the Let's Encrypt certificate automatically.
#
# What this site routes depends on the server's parts (`ROLES` in cloud/.env,
# docs/architecture/scaling.md); cloud_deploy.py and cloud_workers.py write the
# routes into caddy.d/ on every deploy:
#
#   workers.caddy     `/wN/*` → relay worker N (prefix stripped), and a meet's
#                     unprefixed paths → worker 1, which serves any retained meet
#   monitoring.caddy  `/grafana*` → Grafana, when monitoring runs here
#   roles.caddy       `/internal/*` — the workers' API: refused publicly unless
#                     workers on other servers use it (REMOTE_NODES=1) — and the
#                     catch-all: the control plane, or on a workers-only node a
#                     redirect to the meet list
#
# The control plane's catch-all takes `/.well-known/` too. That is load-bearing for
# the QR hand-off (docs/app.md `P-16`) — the control plane serves
# `/.well-known/assetlinks.json` and `/.well-known/apple-app-site-association`, and
# Android fetches the first at install time following **no redirects**. Every
# generated route is a path prefix that cannot match them; one that did would
# swallow them, and the only symptom would be `pm get-app-links
# app.splouch.android` reporting `1024` on a phone, weeks later. Caddy's own ACME
# handler is scoped to `/.well-known/acme-challenge/*` and does not overlap.

# Whole sites cloud_deploy.py adds, such as the monitoring status page on its own
# domain (caddy.d/*.site; none until monitoring is on and given a domain).
import caddy.d/*.site

{$SPLOUCH_DOMAIN} {
    import caddy.d/*.caddy
}
